    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-14172",
      "problem": "What is the range of the function $f(x)$ defined by the graph below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193754/assets/112d92062583c1be3d89a01894feb5f3d7087241cdaec9834c4571be502a9cfd.png)",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the lowest and highest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- The lowest $y$-value is $-1.$ This occurs at the point $(-1,-1).$\n\n- The highest $y$-value is $8.$ This occurs at the point $(2,8).$\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $-1$ and $8,$ including both $-1$ and $8.$\n\nTherefore, the range is \n\n$$\n-1\\leq y \\leq 8,\n$$\n\nwhich can also be written as\n\n$$\n-1\\leq f(x) \\leq 8.\n$$",
